### Work Completed

#### 1. Dead Letter Queue Monitoring Service
Created `app/Services/Messenger/DeadLetterMonitorService.php` with:
- **Statistics Collection**: Total failed messages, by transport, by message class, recent failures (24h), oldest/newest failure timestamps
- **Threshold Alerting**: Configurable threshold (default 10), sends email alert when exceeded
- **Message Inspection**: Get failed messages with pagination for admin UI
- **Retry Capability**: Retry specific failed messages by moving them back to original transport queue
- **Deletion**: Delete specific failed messages
- **Cleanup**: Remove old failed messages based on retention period (default 30 days)
- **Admin UI Support**: Get failed messages grouped by transport/class with counts

#### 2. Cron Job for Dead Letter Monitoring
Created `scripts/cron_dead_letter_monitor.php` with CLI options:
- `--stats`: Show queue statistics (total failed, by transport, by class, recent failures)
- `--cleanup`: Clean up old failed messages (older than retention days)
- `--alert`: Send alert if threshold exceeded
- `--retry-all`: Retry all failed messages (use with caution)

#### 3. Integration with Master Cron Runner
Added Task 16 "Dead Letter Queue Monitor & Cleanup" to `scripts/run_all_crons.php`:
- Runs daily/monthly as part of the master cron
