## Session 387: Phase 4/7 — Identity Unification — Profile Tables Created + Data Migrated (2026-10-23)

### Trigger
User request: "do next" — Continue Phase 4/7 of the platform optimization plan: Identity Unification.

### Work Completed

#### 1. Safety Dump
- `mysqldump -u root apsdreamhome > backups/db/apsdreamhome_pre-identity-unification_2026-10-23.sql` (~87MB, 1 min) — taken before any DB changes per Rule 1.

#### 2. Identity Profile Tables Migration (`database/migrations/create_identity_profile_tables_s387.php`)
Created 4 role-specific profile tables extending the unified `users` table:
- **customer_profiles** — extends users(role='customer') — preferred_location, budget_min/max, property_type, occupation, annual_income, kyc_status, etc.
- **associate_profiles** — extends users(role='associate') — level, referral_code, sponsor_id, brokerage_model, telecaller_*, salary, commission, team_size, etc.
- **employee_profiles** — extends users(role='employee') — employee_code, role, department, designation, salary, pan_number, aadhaar_number, bank details, etc.
- **agent_profiles** — extends users(role='agent') — license_number, experience_years, bank_name, account_number, ifsc_code, etc.

All tables have `user_id BIGINT UNSIGNED` FK → `users(id)` ON DELETE CASCADE, plus appropriate indexes and unique constraints.

#### 3. Data Migration from Legacy Tables
| Source Table | Rows Migrated | Target Table |
|---|---|---|
| `associates` (38 rows, user_id NOT NULL) | 37 | associate_profiles |
| `employees` (17 rows, user_id NOT NULL) | 15 | employee_profiles |
| `agents` (2 rows, user_id NOT NULL) | 2 | agent_profiles |
| `customers` | N/A | No separate table — customers are users with role='customer' |

Rows with NULL user_id were correctly skipped (FK constraint). `INSERT IGNORE` ensures idempotent re-runs.

#### 4. Verification
- All 4 tables created with correct schema
- 57 rows migrated (37 associate + 15 employee + 2 agent)
- 0 errors
- Master test suite: **10/10 SUITES PASSED** (100% HEALTHY, 31.11s)

### Remaining Work (Identity Unification)
1. Update FKs in `bookings`, `leads`, `plot_bookings`, `payments`, etc. to reference `users.id` instead of `associate_id`/`agent_id`/`employee_id`
2. Update controllers/services to use `users` table + profile table lookup instead of direct associates/agents/employees queries
3. Deprecate old tables (keep for backward compatibility, stop writing to them)

