### Key Lessons (carried, continued)
_669. **Always use `data:` named parameter for `api.post()`** — The `ApiService.post()` method signature requires `data:` as a named parameter; passing a map positionally causes "Too many positional arguments" errors.
_670. **Always cast dynamic map values with `?.toString()`** — JSON responses from the backend are `Map<String, dynamic>`; accessing values without explicit `.toString()` causes "dynamic can't be assigned to String" errors.
_671. **Fix in batches, verify per file** — Running `flutter analyze` on individual files after each fix is faster than re-analyzing the whole project repeatedly.
_672. **Zero-error static analysis is achievable with discipline** — 16 errors across 6 files fixed in one round by applying consistent patterns (`data:` parameter + `?.toString()` casts + fixing invalid color constants).
## Session 368: Mobile Deep Scan — Failed Smoke Test Fixed, Township Operations Hub + Solar Subsidy + 11 Web-Only Utility Desks Ported to Mobile (2026-10-21)

### Trigger
User request: "mobile app ko deeply scan kar ke dekho aur kya kya kamiya hai thik karo improve karo aur website me bhi dekh lena kya kya hai jo mobile app me nhi hai usko banao aur improve karo"

### Findings (Deep Scan)
1. **Real bug hidden by the parallel actor's "13/13 tests passing" claim**: `test/widget_test.dart` was failing (`pumpAndSettle timed out` → Pending timers). Root cause: the splash page schedules `Timer(const Duration(seconds: 3), ...)` and the floating AI chatbot pulses on an infinite `AnimationController..repeat()` — neither ever settles, so `pumpAndSettle()` can never complete. The parallel actor's count only included the 2 new suites, not the broken smoke test.
2. **Web-only features absent from mobile**: 11 township utility desks (STP, Borewell/Water, DG Genset, Security Roster, Security Incidents, CCTV, Solid Waste, Horticulture, Street Lighting, Rainwater Harvesting, Fire Safety & NOC) existed only as web admin desks; the mobile app had only Maintenance Dues / Grievances / Site Visit (parallel actor) plus Colony Health (pipeline stages). Also missing: PM Surya Ghar solar subsidy calculator (web has `/customer/solar-calculator`).
3. **Backend gap**: No mobile REST surface for the township utility logs (all 11 tables exist, 0 mobile endpoints).

### Work (All Probe-Verified, 0 Compile Errors, 17/17 Mobile Tests, 10/10 Master, Zero DB Drift)
1. **Fixed `test/widget_test.dart`**: replaced `pumpAndSettle()` with bounded frame pumps + a 3s pump to let the splash timer fire, so no pending timers remain. Asserts no exception + MaterialApp + brand text. Verified green.
2. **New backend controller `app/Http/Controllers/Api/MobileTownshipOpsApiController.php`** (extends BaseController, raw PDO, whitelisted `type`):
   - `GET /api/v2/mobile/township/operations` — consolidated dashboard (11 desks, record_count, colonies_covered, latest_date, latest_headline), fail-open per desk.
   - `GET /api/v2/mobile/township/operations/{type}` — detail with summary + latest 50 records joined to colonies (404 with valid_types list on unknown type).
   - `GET /api/v2/mobile/township/colonies/{id}/utilities` — per-colony coverage (404 if colony missing).
   - `GET /api/v2/mobile/solar/requests` — customer's PM Surya Ghar requests (401 if unauth).
   - Fixed fatal: `jsonResponse()` must be `public` (BaseController contract) — caught via CLI probe.
3. **Routes** (4 new endpoints added in `routes/api.php`).
4. **New mobile pages**:
   - `township_operations_page.dart` — hub grid of 11 desks with live counts + latest headline, pull-to-refresh, honest empty state.
   - `township_utility_detail_page.dart` — per-desk summary + curated field rendering (11 field-maps, generic empty state, colony name per record).
   - `solar_subsidy_page.dart` — full PM Surya Ghar calculator matching the web `SolarSubsidyService` math (capacity from bill, central ₹33k/₹60k/₹78k cap, UP state ₹15k/₹30k, payback, 25-year savings, rooftop feasibility warning) + "My Solar Requests" list.
5. **Integration**: home page tools grid + customer dashboard quick actions (10 tiles incl. Township Ops + Solar Subsidy).
6. **Widget test** `test/township_ops_test.dart` (3 tests) — all green.
7. **Lint cleanup** (7 prefer_const/interpolation infos fixed) on the 3 new pages.

### Verification
- `flutter analyze lib`: **0 errors** (only pre-existing infos/warnings)
- `flutter test`: **17/17 PASS** (widget_test 1 + offline_widgets 12 + township_features 3 + township_ops 3)
- `php -l` clean on controller + routes
- `php testing/master_test_runner.php`: **10/10 SUITES PASSED (100% HEALTHY, 20.36s)**
- Endpoint probe: all 5 endpoints 200/404/401 with correct JSON shape
- MySQL: `users: 117, plots: 756, leads: 38187` (exact 0 drift)
- Temp probes purged.

### Key Lessons (carried, continued)
_665. **A `pumpAndSettle` smoke test is a lie when the app has any infinite animation** — splash spinners and pulsing FABs never settle. Pump bounded frames and assert no exception + brand present instead; that's the honest boot test.
_666. **A parallel actor's "N/N tests passing" claim must be re-run, not trusted** — the previous round's 13/13 count excluded the broken `widget_test.dart` (1 failing). Always run the full suite, not just the named ones.
_667. **Child method visibility must match the parent contract** — `BaseController::jsonResponse()` is `public`; declaring it `private` in the child is a fatal error that surfaces as a generic 500. Match visibility (and check the parent signature) before writing.
_668. **Probe the endpoint, not just the controller** — CLI construction passed while HTTP 500'd on a visibility mismatch. A live HTTP probe is the only thing that catches router→controller wiring.

