4. **Redis** — Install on office PC when multi-server scaling needed

### Key Lessons (carried, continued)
_656. **Gemini Vision API uses inline_data for image input** — The `inline_data` field with `mime_type` and `data` (base64) is the standard way to send images to Gemini. Other providers (Groq, OpenRouter) support vision via OpenAI-compatible format with `image_url` field.
_657. **Photo-based lead creation needs AI analysis + structured extraction** — Send image to vision model with a structured prompt requesting JSON output, then parse the response to populate lead fields. Fallback to empty analysis if vision unavailable.
_658. **Visit confirmation with photos creates audit trail** — Store photos in visit-specific directory, run AI analysis on each, update visit status, advance linked lead. Photos serve as evidence for registry/legal purposes.
_659. **Mobile image upload needs base64 encoding** — Flutter's `image_picker` returns file path; read bytes, base64 encode, send as JSON field. Keep image under 1MB (maxWidth/maxHeight 1024, quality 80) to avoid payload size issues.
_660. **Dart collection if elements need proper context** — `if (condition) widget` inside `children: []` works, but `if (condition) ...[...]` spread syntax is more reliable. Always verify with `dart analyze` after writing collection literals.

'''
